{
    "background_story": "Dulce was a brilliant and resourceful young woman who grew up in a small village plagued by frequent power outages. Despite the unlighted streets and homes, Dulce found ways to thrive in the darkness. She developed a keen sense of spatial awareness and learned to navigate the village with ease, even in the blackest of nights. Dulce's resourcefulness inspired her to create innovative solutions to the village's energy crisis. She designed and built sustainable lanterns using recycled materials, providing a reliable source of light for her community. As the village began to flourish, Dulce's determination and creativity in the face of adversity earned her the nickname 'La Luz en la Oscuridad' - The Light in the Darkness.",
